{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-2759","published":"2026-06-24T11:11:41Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:21:11.157285156Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-3592"],"summary":"dhcp security update","details":"The Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP) is a network management protocol used on UDP/IP networks whereby a DHCP server dynamically assigns an IP address and other network configuration parameters to each device on a network so they can communicate with other IP networks.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nBIND resolvers are vulnerable to an amplified resource consumption/exhaustion attack.  If a victim resolver makes a query to a specially crafted zone, the resolver will consume disproportionate resources.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.16.50, 9.18.0 through 9.18.48, 9.20.0 through 9.20.22, 9.21.0 through 9.21.21, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.16.50-S1, 9.18.11-S1 through 9.18.48-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.22-S1.(CVE-2026-3592)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"dhcp","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/dhcp&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["dhcp-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","dhcp-debuginfo-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","dhcp-debugsource-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","dhcp-devel-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["dhcp-help-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["dhcp-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["dhcp-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","dhcp-debuginfo-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","dhcp-debugsource-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","dhcp-devel-4.4.2-17.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-2759.json"}},{"package":{"name":"dhcp","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/dhcp&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.4.3-12.oe2203sp4"